# admin.withclaude.in — environment
#
# Copy to `admin/.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; never commit real
# values, and never commit a real editor's email address either — accounts are
# created by running `npm run db:create-user` against the database.
#
# ── THE ONE RULE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Nothing here is ever prefixed `PUBLIC_`. Astro inlines any `PUBLIC_*`
# variable into the browser bundle, so a `PUBLIC_BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` would let
# any visitor forge a session. `db/env.ts` refuses to start if such a variable
# exists, and `tests/admin-isolation.test.ts` checks the built output.


# ── DATABASE (required) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The SAME database as the public site. There is one schema, one set of
# migrations, and one `DATABASE_URL` — the admin does not get its own copy of
# anything.
#
# The driver is chosen from the host: a `*.neon.tech` URL uses Neon's
# serverless driver, anything else uses node-postgres over TCP. That is what
# lets the admin run against a PostgreSQL on localhost, which matters because
# the admin cannot do anything at all without a database.
#
#   Production:  postgresql://user:pass@ep-x-123.region.aws.neon.tech/withclaude?sslmode=require
#   Local:       postgresql://postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/withclaude_dev
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/withclaude_dev"


# ── AUTHENTICATION (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Signs session cookies. Rotating it signs everybody out, which is the correct
# emergency response to a suspected leak.
#
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""

# The admin's own origin, with no trailing slash. Three things read it:
#
#   · magic-link URLs are built from it, so a wrong value emails a broken link
#   · it is the only trusted origin for state-changing requests (CSRF)
#   · `assertSameOrigin()` compares every POST's Origin against it
#
# It must match how the admin is actually reached, exactly.
#
#   Production:  https://admin.withclaude.in
#   Local:       http://localhost:4322
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:4322"


# ── SIGN-IN EMAIL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Resend sends the magic link. Unlike the public site's acknowledgement — where
# losing the email is better than losing the submission — the link IS the
# sign-in, so a failure here is a locked door.
#
# WITHOUT THESE, IN DEVELOPMENT: the link is printed to the server console and
# the log says so. Nothing pretends to have been sent, and you can sign in
# offline by copying it out of the terminal.
#
# WITHOUT THESE, IN PRODUCTION: sign-in fails loudly rather than showing
# somebody "check your inbox" for a message that is never coming.
#
# RESEND_FROM must be an address on a domain verified in Resend.
RESEND_API_KEY=""
RESEND_FROM="WITH CLAUDE <hello@withclaude.in>"
# Optional. Where a reply to a sign-in email goes.
RESEND_REPLY_TO=""


# ── NOT USED, AND DELIBERATELY ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# SUBMISSION_IP_SALT belongs to the public site's `/api/submit`. The admin
# never hashes an address because it never stores one.
#
# Vercel Blob is the planned media store for Phase 4. It is not configured,
# not installed, and not referenced anywhere — a dependency added for a phase
# that has not started is how a phase boundary stops meaning anything.
